  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      202.73,
      397.2,
      331.07
    ],
    "text": "4.Subject to the provisions of this Act and any otherwritten law, the Corporation shall have the power to do,perform and execute all such acts, matters and thingswhatsoever, as are necessary and desirable for the promotionor furtherance of the objects of the Corporation, or any oneof them, including the power to open, operate and closebank accounts, to borrow or raise money, with or withoutsecurity, to receive or collect grants and donations, to investits funds, and to engage, employ and dismiss officers andservants required for the carrying out of the objects of theCorporation.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      343.13,
      397.19,
      401.27
    ],
    "text": "5.(1) The affairs of the Corporation shall, subject to therules of the Corporation, be administered by a Board ofDirectors consisting of such number of members as may beprovided for rules made in that behalf and elected inaccordance therewith.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      413.33,
      397.2,
      459.83
    ],
    "text": "(2) The first Board of Directors of the Corporation shallbe the members of the Board of Directors holding office onthe day immediately preceding the date of commencementof this Act.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      471.89,
      397.21,
      553.43
    ],
    "text": "6.(1) It shall be lawful for the Corporation, from timeto time, at any general meeting of the Corporation andby the majority of not less than three-fourths of theActive Members of the Corporation present and voting, tomake rules, not inconsistant with the provision of this Act,or any other written law, for the management of the affairs ofthe Corporation and the accomplishment of its objects.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      565.49,
      397.19,
      623.63
    ],
    "text": "(2) The rules of the Association in force on the date ofcommencement of this Act, in so far as they are notinconsistent with the provisions of this Act, or any otherwritten law, shall be deemed to be rules made by theCorporation under this Act.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      635.69,
      397.19,
      670.79
    ],
    "text": "(3) Any rule made y the Corportion may be amended orrescinded in like manner as a rule may by made undersubsection (1).",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      403.15,
      343.75,
      448.88,
      381.62
    ],
